---
import BaseLayout from '../../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const locale = 'en';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Manufacturing & Production — BOM, Production Orders, Quality Control"
  description="Bill of materials, recipe management, production orders, work-in-progress tracking, quality control, batch certification, and yield analysis. Part of Kraal Code ERP."
  locale={locale}
  canonicalUrl="https://kraalcode.com/en/capabilities/manufacturing/"
>
  <section class="page-hero section--warm">
    <div class="container">
      <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><ol><li><a href="/en/">Home</a></li><li><a href="/en/capabilities/">Capabilities</a></li><li aria-current="page">Manufacturing & Production</li></ol></nav>
      <h1>Manufacturing & Production</h1>
      <p class="page-hero-subtext">From recipe to finished goods. Track raw materials, production orders, quality inspections, and yield — with every cost posted to the ledger automatically.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section"><div class="container container--narrow">
    <h2>Who this is for</h2>
    <p>Factory managers, production supervisors, quality controllers, and business owners who manufacture or process goods. Whether you run a food processing plant, a packaging line, or a workshop, this module manages the production lifecycle from raw material to finished product.</p>
    <p>If your business transforms raw materials into saleable goods — and you need to track what went in, what came out, what it cost, and whether it passed quality inspection — this module gives you that control without a separate manufacturing system.</p>
  </div></section>

  <section class="section section--warm"><div class="container">
    <h2>What you can do</h2>
    <div class="feature-grid">
      <div class="feature-card"><h3>Recipe / BOM Management</h3><p>Define bills of materials (recipes) with ingredients, quantities, expected yields, and processing steps. Support single-output and multi-output recipes. Version control for recipe changes.</p></div>
      <div class="feature-card"><h3>Production Orders</h3><p>Create production orders against recipes. Specify planned quantity, start date, and work centre. Track status from planned to started to completed. Support partial completions.</p></div>
      <div class="feature-card"><h3>Work-in-Progress Tracking</h3><p>Track materials consumed and costs accumulated during production. Post WIP entries to the general ledger. Close WIP on production completion with variance analysis.</p></div>
      <div class="feature-card"><h3>Quality Control</h3><p>Define inspection templates with checkpoints and acceptance criteria. Record inspection results against production batches. Approve or reject batches based on QC findings.</p></div>
      <div class="feature-card"><h3>Batch Certification</h3><p>Certify production batches for release. Record certification authority, date, and conditions. Only certified batches move to finished goods inventory.</p></div>
      <div class="feature-card"><h3>Yield Analysis</h3><p>Compare planned vs actual yields. Track waste, scrap, and by-products. Identify production inefficiencies. Generate yield variance reports by product and period.</p></div>
      <div class="feature-card"><h3>Worker Management</h3><p>Track factory workers, their skills, attendance, and assignments to production orders. Manage shift schedules and labour cost allocation to production batches.</p></div>
      <div class="feature-card"><h3>Materials Requisition</h3><p>Request raw materials for production. Route through approval workflows. Track material consumption against planned quantities and flag variances.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="section"><div class="container container--narrow">
    <h2>How it connects</h2>
    <p>Manufacturing consumes raw materials and produces finished goods. Every movement posts to inventory and accounting automatically:</p>
    <ul class="connection-list">
      <li><strong>Inventory</strong> → raw materials consumed, finished goods received on production completion</li>
      <li><strong>Accounting</strong> → WIP, COGS, and variance postings automatic on order close</li>
      <li><strong>Procurement</strong> → material requirements trigger purchase requests when stock is low</li>
      <li><strong>HR</strong> → worker assignments and labour cost tracking per production order</li>
      <li><strong>Quality Control</strong> → inspection results gate batch release to finished goods</li>
    </ul>
  </div></section>

  <section class="section section--warm"><div class="container container--narrow">
    <h2>Controls and permissions</h2>
    <div class="controls-grid">
      <div class="control-item"><h3>Batch Release Authority</h3><p>Only quality controllers can release certified batches. Production supervisors can initiate orders but cannot release finished goods without QC sign-off.</p></div>
      <div class="control-item"><h3>Material Consumption Limits</h3><p>Material requisitions are checked against recipe quantities. Excess consumption requires supervisor approval with documented reason. Variances are flagged for review.</p></div>
      <div class="control-item"><h3>Production Cost Lock</h3><p>Production orders are costed on completion. Once closed, costs are locked and posted to the ledger. Reopening requires finance approval and creates an audit entry.</p></div>
      <div class="control-item"><h3>Audit Trail</h3><p>Every production order, material requisition, QC inspection, and batch certification is logged with user, timestamp, and IP. INSERT-only records. No production data can be silently altered.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="section"><div class="container">
    <h2>See it in action</h2>
    <p class="screenshot-intro">Screenshots from the live Kraal Code system — coming soon.</p>
    <div class="screenshot-grid">
      <div class="screenshot-slot"><div class="screenshot-placeholder"><span class="screenshot-label">Recipe Builder</span><span class="screenshot-note">Live product screenshot — coming soon</span></div></div>
      <div class="screenshot-slot"><div class="screenshot-placeholder"><span class="screenshot-label">Production Orders</span><span class="screenshot-note">Live product screenshot — coming soon</span></div></div>
      <div class="screenshot-slot"><div class="screenshot-placeholder"><span class="screenshot-label">Quality Inspection</span><span class="screenshot-note">Live product screenshot — coming soon</span></div></div>
      <div class="screenshot-slot"><div class="screenshot-placeholder"><span class="screenshot-label">Yield Analysis</span><span class="screenshot-note">Live product screenshot — coming soon</span></div></div>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="section--dark section"><div class="container text-center">
    <h2>See manufacturing in action</h2>
    <p>Request a demonstration tailored to your production and manufacturing needs.</p>
    <a href="/en/contact/" class="btn btn--inverse">Request a Demonstration →</a>
  </div></section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page-hero {
    padding: var(--kc-space-20) 0 var(--kc-space-12);
  }
  .page-hero h1 {
    font-size: var(--kc-text-4xl);
    max-width: 700px;
  }
  .page-hero-subtext {
    font-size: var(--kc-text-lg);
    color: var(--kc-text-secondary);
    max-width: 60ch;
    margin-top: var(--kc-space-4);
  }
  .breadcrumb ol {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    display: flex;
    gap: var(--kc-space-2);
    font-size: var(--kc-text-sm);
    color: var(--kc-text-tertiary);
    margin-bottom: var(--kc-space-6);
  }
  .breadcrumb a {
    color: var(--kc-teal);
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .breadcrumb li:not(:last-child)::after {
    content: '/';
    margin-left: var(--kc-space-2);
    color: var(--kc-text-tertiary);
  }
  .container--narrow {
    max-width: var(--kc-container-narrow);
  }
  .container--narrow p {
    font-size: var(--kc-text-base);
    color: var(--kc-text-secondary);
    line-height: var(--kc-leading-relaxed);
    margin-bottom: var(--kc-space-4);
  }
  .feature-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: var(--kc-space-6);
    margin-top: var(--kc-space-8);
  }
  .feature-card {
    padding: var(--kc-space-6);
    background: var(--kc-surface-light);
    border: 1px solid var(--kc-border-subtle);
    border-radius: var(--kc-radius-lg);
  }
  .feature-card h3 {
    font-size: var(--kc-text-lg);
    font-family: var(--kc-font-body);
    font-weight: var(--kc-weight-semibold);
    margin-bottom: var(--kc-space-2);
  }
  .feature-card p {
    font-size: var(--kc-text-sm);
    color: var(--kc-text-secondary);
  }
  .connection-list {
    margin-top: var(--kc-space-4);
  }
  .connection-list li {
    margin-bottom: var(--kc-space-3);
    font-size: var(--kc-text-base);
    color: var(--kc-text-secondary);
  }
  .connection-list strong {
    color: var(--kc-text-primary);
  }
  .controls-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: var(--kc-space-6);
    margin-top: var(--kc-space-6);
  }
  .control-item {
    padding: var(--kc-space-5);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--kc-teal);
  }
  .control-item h3 {
    font-size: var(--kc-text-base);
    font-family: var(--kc-font-body);
    font-weight: var(--kc-weight-semibold);
    margin-bottom: var(--kc-space-1);
  }
  .control-item p {
    font-size: var(--kc-text-sm);
    color: var(--kc-text-secondary);
  }
  .screenshot-intro {
    color: var(--kc-text-secondary);
    margin-bottom: var(--kc-space-6);
  }
  .screenshot-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: var(--kc-space-6);
  }
  .screenshot-placeholder {
    aspect-ratio: 16 / 10;
    background: var(--kc-surface-warm);
    border: 2px dashed var(--kc-border);
    border-radius: var(--kc-radius-lg);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: var(--kc-space-2);
  }
  .screenshot-label {
    font-weight: var(--kc-weight-semibold);
    color: var(--kc-text-primary);
  }
  .screenshot-note {
    font-size: var(--kc-text-sm);
    color: var(--kc-text-tertiary);
  }
  .btn--inverse {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    padding: var(--kc-space-4) var(--kc-space-8);
    font-weight: var(--kc-weight-semibold);
    font-size: var(--kc-text-base);
    border-radius: var(--kc-radius-lg);
    background: transparent;
    color: var(--kc-text-inverse);
    border: 2px solid var(--kc-teal-light);
    transition: all var(--kc-transition-fast);
    text-decoration: none;
    margin-top: var(--kc-space-6);
  }
  .btn--inverse:hover {
    background: var(--kc-teal);
    border-color: var(--kc-teal);
  }
  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .page-hero h1 {
      font-size: var(--kc-text-3xl);
    }
    .feature-grid,
    .controls-grid,
    .screenshot-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
